  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting material is equiatomic CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy has acceptable tribological performance at room temperature.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy develops increased friction and wear at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is addition of approximately 5–10 at.% Ti to CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 is a relevant example of the proposed modified composition.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti addition will enable in-situ formation of a stable titanium-containing oxide phase on the sliding surface from 25 °C to 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide formed by the Ti-modified alloy will be lubricious.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will contain dispersed nanometric Ti-based precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sliding will produce a continuous, coherent surface oxide layer consisting of TiO2 or mixed oxides.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At lower temperatures, the Ti-modified alloy will retain its microstructural integrity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, preferential oxidation associated with Ti will form a protective oxide film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The surface oxide film will minimize direct metal-to-metal contact and reduce interfacial shear stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced direct contact and shear stress will decrease the coefficient of friction and wear rate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to unmodified CoCrFeNi, the Ti-modified alloy will have a lower coefficient of friction at both room temperature and elevated temperatures up to 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to unmodified CoCrFeNi, the Ti-modified alloy will have a lower wear rate throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atmospheric oxidation can generate a protective oxide layer that increases the elevated-temperature wear resistance of AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coefficient of friction of AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 decreases slightly as test temperature increases.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxide-formation kinetics will be active under ambient-air sliding at approximately 1 N throughout the stated 25–800 °C boundary.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    }
  ],
